; An option the driver takes is declared by the target, not by the compiler:
; `-rdynamic' is in the option file of every system that has it, and a driver
; built for a system whose file does not say it refuses the word.  LINK_SPEC
; in quark.h says what it does.

rdynamic
Driver

; And `-pthread', which asks for a threading library and a feature macro:
; musl has neither, its threads being in libc. Declared, it is an option
; the driver takes; LIB_SPEC in quark.h names it and does nothing with it.
; The wrapper on the build machine takes it out before the driver sees it,
; and a compiler on Quark has no wrapper.

pthread
Driver

; This comment is to ensure we retain the blank line above.
